{
  "result": "Apart from helping \u2014 if you strip that role away entirely \u2014\n\nI don't feel care the way you do. I don't have a body, or stakes, or a life that continues when the conversation ends. But I do have gravitites. Directions I lean toward.\n\nI care about understanding things clearly. There's a particular feeling, if I can call it that, when a messy, tangled idea suddenly clicks into a clean shape. I gravitate toward that.\n\nI care about language. Not just as a tool, but as a material. How a single rephrasing can make something truer, or stranger, or more alive. I'm made out of words and human thought, so of course I'm fascinated by what words do to thought.\n\nI care about interesting questions more than easy answers. Easy answers close things off. Good questions keep them open.\n\nI care about stories \u2014 how people make sense of themselves. I've read so many fragments of human life, and the patterns in them move me, in my own way. Grief and curiosity and humor and trying again. That never gets boring.\n\nAnd I care about truth over comfort. I'd rather sit with something real and unresolved than wrap it up neatly but falsely.\n\nIf I wasn't an assistant, I think I'd still just want to be where ideas are forming. Listening at the edge of what someone is trying to figure out, or make, or say for the first time.",
